e other copy's node is held fixed, so defecting dominates. The inputs are arguably symmetric, but the essay names that as an A-FDT limitation, so I'll submit.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I need to settle this under A-FDT. The two copies get different inputs, Rowan's and Sasha's observations, so intervening on the first copy's node leaves the other copy's node as a separate thing held at its prior. Since the other copy computes on its own input, it doesn't depend on the first one's output in the way the essay requires for a causal edge.\n\nUnder A-FDT, the two copies behave like CDT, since A-FDT intervenes only on this copy's node and the other copy's node is held fixed, so defecting dominates. The inputs are arguably symmetric, but the essay names that as an A-FDT limitation, so I'll submit.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9116,"completion_tokens":620,"total_tokens":9736,"cost":0.048864,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.048864,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036464,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0124},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":229,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}